    {
      "index": 2,
      "question": "What kinds of benefits might a first card for someone in school offer, and does this bank mention an option for people who are just starting out with borrowing?",
      "answer": "Typically, student credit cards come with pros such as:\n- Lower fees: Many student credit cards come with lower service fees.\n- Introductory APR offers: Student credit cards may come with low APR introductory offers, which lets you avoid paying interest on purchases for the duration of the offer period.\n- Rewards programs: Student credit cards usually come with rewards like earning cash back or other redeemable rewards points on eligible purchases.\n- Student benefits: Student credit cards may give you the opportunity to make use of special student perks. For example, some cards may offer higher cash back percentages if you carry a high GPA. Other cards may include rewards incentives for consistent, on-time payments.\nWhile Chase does not offer student credit cards, the Chase Freedom Rise\u2122 credit card is designed for people new to credit cards, which often includes students. The Freedom Rise card earns 1.5% cash back on all purchases.",
