    {
      "index": 3,
      "question": "How long is a paper payment from someone's bank account usually still usable, and what should I do before trying to cash one that's pretty old?",
      "answer": "It\u2019s typical for personal checks to expire after six months. This time frame is laid out in the Uniform Commercial Code (UCC), a set of laws that govern commercial transactions in the United States. After six months, it\u2019s generally at the bank\u2019s discretion whether a personal check is considered expired. If you\u2019re cashing older checks, it may make sense to contact the issuer first. Perhaps they could re-issue the check or confirm they can still honor it.",
